    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0143" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">330/12–1151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Peurifoy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-11T11:00:00+02:00">December 11,
                            1951—11 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2700. This morning Plastiras sent Moatsis, chief of PriMin’s polit bureau, to tell me that if Greece’s candidacy for
                        SC is proving at all embarrassing for us in
                    our relations with UK or others PriMin wld
                    immed issue orders withdrawing Greece from race.</p>
                <p>Moatsis emphasized Plastiras’ intense desire for complete cooperation with us
                    particularly in foreign affairs. He added that PriMin had been intensely irritated by Politis’ activities in early
                        GA meetings, and wished us to know that he
                    disapproved of any maneuvering by Grk rep which wld not be wholly in accord with
                    Amer wishes.</p>
                <pb facs="0144" n="122" xml:id="pg122"/>
                <p>Wld appreciate immed telegraphic advice so that I may answer Plastiras.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d72-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sent priority Dept 2700; rptd info Paris 72 for
                        USDel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peurifoy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d72-f1" n="1" xml:id="d72-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 2804, December 11, 7:36 p. m. (repeated for information to Paris as
                        Gadel 419) the Department responded:
                    “Inform Plastiras that Greek candidacy not proving embarrassing to U.S. from
                    standpoint our relations with U.K. and that U.S. intends vote for Greece during
                    balloting scheduled December 13.” (330/12–1151)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
